#!/usr/bin/env python3
# demiurge-touch-test — fullscreen touch mirror + smartboard-style calibrator.
#
# Two modes, same polished visual language (dark, glow, 800x480 KMSDRM):
#
#   mirror mode (default when a calibration exists)
#     Up to 4 simultaneous touches (SDL FINGERDOWN/MOTION/UP) with glowing
#     circles, trails, ripples and a live readout. If a calibration exists it
#     is APPLIED to the mirrored position, so "finger != crosshair" errors are
#     visibly fixed. Hold the top-left corner 5 s (or ESC/Q) to exit; hold the
#     top-right "CAL" corner 1.5 s to enter calibration.
#
#   calibration mode (auto when no calibration exists, or --calibrate,
#   or the CAL corner)
#     Five targets (4 corners inset 40 px + center). Tap and hold each one
#     briefly; RAW evdev coordinates are read straight from the touch device
#     (bypassing SDL and any existing calibration) and averaged. A point is
#     accepted only from a stable press (jitter-checked); wild outliers are
#     re-asked. From the 5 points an affine raw→screen mapping is fitted per
#     axis — including axis-swap and inversion detection from the corner
#     geometry, so the mapping survives future rotation changes. A verify
#     screen then shows a crosshair tracking the finger WITH the calibration
#     applied: tap ✓ to save, ✗ to redo.
#
#     Cancel at any time: ESC/Q, or press-and-hold anywhere ≥4 s (a red arc
#     appears after 2 s). Cancelling NEVER touches an existing calibration
#     file — the file is written only on a completed run confirmed with ✓.
#
# Persistence + consumers (see demiurge/docs/config-reference.md):
#   ~/demiurge/touch-cal.conf        key=value, written atomically on ✓ only
#   demiurge-touch daemon            reloads it automatically (mtime / SIGHUP)
#   this program's mirror mode       applies it live
#   SDL apps (NEPTR UI)              get it via a udev hwdb EVDEV_ABS entry
#     (/etc/udev/hwdb.d/61-demiurge-touch-cal.hwdb) that the calibrator stages
#     with sudo -n on save: it rewrites the kernel-advertised axis ranges,
#     which is what SDL's evdev layer scales by. Applied immediately (udevadm
#     trigger) for newly-opened devices and persistent across reboots. The
#     ads7846 overlay xmin/xmax/... params in config.txt are IGNORED by the
#     current kernel (verified: kernel advertises 0-4095 regardless), so the
#     equivalent overlay line is only printed/staged for reference.
#
# Runs on the Pi console via SDL KMSDRM (same stack as the NEPTR UI):
#   sudo systemctl stop neptr-ui
#   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=kmsdrm demiurge-touch-test [--calibrate|--mirror]
#   sudo systemctl start neptr-ui        # normal UI back

